    "Every code database entry whose parameters carry the R8 role (plan section 7.2 CodeParam.position, 7.16 #106; roadmap R8, accepted 2026-10-01): one list per database file, in file order, each row the entry's parameters in order with the role each declares (null: not reviewed). Written by the M10 prelude P10.",
    "src/lib/data/codes/positions.test.ts holds the shipped files to this list and the TypeScript reader positionOf to the roles; tests/python/test_code_positions.py holds gedit_nc.position_of to the same roles. A role cannot be added, dropped or changed without this file changing, and so without a reviewer reading it (gate G10).",
    "tool-axis = an absolute coordinate on the tool axis, which a shift on the tool axis moves with the axis words (Z while the plane is XY; any other plane refuses). none = reviewed, no absolute position. other = an absolute position the role does not cover: the block is refused and listed. mode = a mode argument; absent, empty or 0 keeps the reading, any other value refuses the call. An axis word (X, Y, Z of a Fanuc cycle) carries no role: it moves as an axis word.",
    "Not listed, and so refused by address arithmetic as not reviewed: every other cycle (the Fanuc lathe's own drilling cycles G83 to G89, whose R is a machine-parameter question; Okuma G181-G189; the Sinumerik turning cycles other than CYCLE93 and CYCLE97, the pattern cycles and the milling cycles not listed here; a Klartext cycle the database lacks, which falls to the generic CYCL DEF, among them cycle 20 CONTOUR DATA, whose Q5 and Q7 are tool-axis positions of a cycle that acts where it is defined). B1 (a7s) added the Sinumerik milling cycles CYCLE61, POCKET3, POCKET4, SLOT1 and the turning cycles CYCLE93, CYCLE97 (their positions in the plane are other, so a call is refused and listed), and the Klartext cycles 21 to 25, 251 to 254, 256 and 257. SLOT2 (its circle centre _CPA, _CPO is other) and CYCLE72 (its contour, named by _KNAME, is a set of positions elsewhere, so _KNAME is other) were added from the manuals on 2026-10-12.",
    "P4a integration (plan section 7 #305, #301): the Fanuc lathe's multiple repetitive cycles G70 to G76 are reviewed from the FANUC 30i lathe operator's manual: their parameters are depths, retracts, allowances, block numbers, counts and feeds (none), their X and Z end points (G74 to G76) are axis words and U, W are increments or allowances read as the block says; the profile blocks P to Q are ordinary moves. CYCLE95 names its contour by NPP (a subprogram or a part of the program), which is other like _KNAME of CYCLE72. Klartext PATTERN DEF is nothing but positions of its own (other)."
  ],
